---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '../../lib/url';
---
<Base
  title="Editorial and affiliate policy"
  description="How this site handles money, why there are no product links on life-safety pages, and why there are no STIHL links at all."
>
  <div class="shell railed flow pol">
    <span class="rail-mark" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
    <h1>Editorial and affiliate policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Written as a public commitment so it can be held against us.
    </p>

    <h2>The rules</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <b>Commission never influences what is recommended or the order it appears in.</b>
        Gear is specified by the standard it has to meet first — ASTM F1897 chaps, a
        semi-chisel chain in the right pitch and gauge — and products come second, as
        examples of that specification.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>No commercial links on life-safety pages.</b> Power lines, PPE and the buddy
        rule, kickback, storm hazards, felling, and anything about what to do when
        someone is bleeding: those pages carry no affiliate links, no sponsor mentions,
        and nothing to buy. They are marked “life-safety page — no product links” at the
        top.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Disclosure at the top of the page, not buried in the footer.</b> Any page with
        affiliate links says so in plain language before the content starts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>A local dealer is listed alongside any online option.</b> Every time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>No paid reviews, no sponsored placements in content, no ranking for payment.</b>
        If a sponsor ever appears on this site, it will be as a named sponsor in a fixed
        place, not woven into a recommendation.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why there are no STIHL product links anywhere</h2>
    <p>
      STIHL sells through its authorized dealer network and dealers are not permitted to
      sell new STIHL products online outside STIHL's own structure. There is no US
      affiliate program to join.
    </p>
    <p>
      The practical consequence is the part that matters to you: the STIHL saws listed on
      general online marketplaces are third-party stock, frequently gray-market, and
      typically carry no manufacturer warranty. Sending you to one of those would earn
      this site a commission and leave you with a worse saw and no support.
    </p>
    <p>
      So the <a href={u('/reference/stihl/')}>STIHL page</a> links to dealers and to
      nothing else. That is not a favour — it is the only honest version of that page.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the money would come from, if there is any</h2>
    <p>
      Being specific about this is part of the policy.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Consumables.</b> Chains, files, bar oil, fuel cans, wedges, chaps, helmets,
        trauma kits. Things people genuinely need, replace often, and mostly buy at the
        wrong specification — which is exactly where a standards-first recommendation
        helps rather than distorts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Arborist suppliers</b> where they carry the gear the big retailers do not.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Local sponsorship.</b> A Kaua‘i dealer or rental yard sponsoring the site
        outright is worth more than a year of affiliate clicks and is more honest. If
        that happens, it will be named plainly on this page and nowhere else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Grants and partnerships</b> — county, resilience funding, a VOAD partnership.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      As of this writing the site earns nothing and has no affiliate relationships in
      place. When that changes, this page changes first.
    </p>

    <h2>No tracking, and why that is a policy and not a boast</h2>
    <p>
      No cookies, no analytics, no ad networks, no third-party scripts. Partly on
      principle, partly because it has to work offline and every third-party request is
      something that fails at the exact moment somebody needs this page in Wailua
      Homesteads with no bars.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and conflicts</h2>
    <p>
      If you think a recommendation here is shaped by money rather than by what works,
      say so in public: <a href="https://github.com/mechaloctopus/chainsaw/issues">open
      an issue</a>. The whole site is in that repository, including this page's history.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .pol { padding-top: 2rem; }
  .pol h2 { font-size: var(--text-h3); }
</style>
